; A composition fixture, and the only one in the bag. Every OTHER Control scene
; here isolates one type against a flat backdrop; this one wires 23 of them into
; a single settings/HUD panel and therefore moves many variables at once ON
; PURPOSE. It can never localise a regression — a shifted pixel here could be
; the split solve, the box flow, a stylebox content margin, a font metric or the
; canvas snap, and the frame cannot say which. That is not a defect of the
; scene, it is its subject: the interactions BETWEEN containers have no other
; witness, because a single-variable scene has, by construction, nothing to
; interact with. A regression seen here is localised in the unit-* fixture that
; owns the type, and that is still where a fix is pinned.
;
; What only composition can reach:
;
;   * a chain of containers solving one after another — MarginContainer feeds
;     HSplitContainer feeds VBoxContainer feeds ScrollContainer feeds
;     PanelContainer feeds MarginContainer feeds GridContainer, and each link
;     passes down a rect the next one has to re-solve. A minimum-size that
;     propagates the wrong way up shows only when there is something above it.
;   * a widget sized by a container instead of by its own offsets — the sliders,
;     the OptionButton and the LineEdit here have no rect of their own at all.
;   * modulate multiplying down a nesting chain: Actions carries alpha, Back
;     inside it carries a tint, and the button must show the product.
;   * stylebox content margins nesting inside container separations, which is
;     the pair that double-counts.
;   * a ScrollContainer that actually overflows, so the clip edge and the
;     scrollbar exist. Everything above the fold is deliberate; only Keybinds
;     runs past it, and it carries no type that is not already visible.
;   * a CanvasLayer drawing OVER the whole Control tree rather than beside it.
;   * a SubViewportContainer sampling a Control subtree — Controls inside a
;     render target, not world content.
;   * wrapped text in two engines (Label autowrap, RichTextLabel BBCode spans)
;     inside containers whose width the layout decides, so the wrap point is a
;     layout output rather than an authored constant.
;
; Deterministic by construction: no animation, no particles, no timers, no
; random seed, nothing time-dependent — the picture at settle 0 is the only
; picture this scene has.
;
; Theme overrides are here because the composition needs them, not for coverage:
; the styleboxes give the cards their plates and their content margins (the
; thing that has to nest correctly against the separations), the separation and
; margin constants set the rhythm the flow has to reproduce, and the font size
; and colour overrides on the title, the subtitle and the brief are what make
; the panel readable as a hierarchy. No Theme resource is applied, so every
; unstyled widget resolves through the bundled default theme.
;
; Control itself draws no ink: the root and Actions/Spacer are pure layout.

